1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,666
Alrighty, guys.

2
00:00:01,666 --> 00:00:03,000
Welcome, welcome.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,600
Thank you for being here.

4
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:07,800
I am so happy to see you guys back.

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:11,866
I'm happy
to see a lot of new names in the chat.

6
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,266
That's great!

7
00:00:14,266 --> 00:00:17,133
So let's get started.

8
00:00:17,133 --> 00:00:21,733
Well today,
we are talking about IWP Ready Assets

9
00:00:21,733 --> 00:00:24,733
and how to make them.

10
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:29,433
And hello! For everybody
who do not know me,

11
00:00:29,466 --> 00:00:30,833
let me introduce myself.

12
00:00:30,833 --> 00:00:33,000
My name is SpaceGlitterUnicorn.

13
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,700
I am the creator of Fairies in the Trees,
and I'm also a collaborator on a lot of

14
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:43,800
wonderful worlds made by
a lot of people in the community.

15
00:00:44,366 --> 00:00:47,700
A lot of fantastic creators

16
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:52,833
in our Horizon Worlds.

17
00:00:53,366 --> 00:00:56,400
Okay, so first
we're going to go over the Skills Matrix,

18
00:00:56,900 --> 00:01:01,066
and then we're going to go over
what makes a good IWP item.

19
00:01:01,666 --> 00:01:04,066
And yeah, let's talk about it.

20
00:01:04,066 --> 00:01:07,700
Next after
that would be the basic asset blockout.

21
00:01:08,033 --> 00:01:12,700
Kind of like blocking out the object,
making sure that we have the right—

22
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,366
the right

23
00:01:15,366 --> 00:01:19,833
ratio throughout the whole model.
It’s really easy

24
00:01:19,833 --> 00:01:23,200
and really will help you solidify

25
00:01:23,766 --> 00:01:26,766
your build following through.

26
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:29,000
Keeping it simple.

27
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,400
After that, we're going
to finalize the design and have it

28
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:36,700
ready to be imported into Horizon.
In the Skill Matrix,

29
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:39,800
basically this

30
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,800
session will be in the art domain.

31
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:47,633
And the subset,
the subdomain, would be the assets.

32
00:01:47,866 --> 00:01:50,233
And this is important info.

33
00:01:50,233 --> 00:01:52,333
This session is recorded.

34
00:01:52,333 --> 00:01:53,300
Don't be afraid.

35
00:01:53,300 --> 00:01:56,600
Do not be afraid to ask any questions.

36
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:59,800
Use the Discord chat and stay engaged.

37
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,166
Teamwork makes the dream work.

38
00:02:02,166 --> 00:02:05,166
So please, definitely in the chat,
help each other.

39
00:02:06,066 --> 00:02:08,866
We are a fantastic community

40
00:02:08,866 --> 00:02:12,266
and seriously,
if you have a question,

41
00:02:12,266 --> 00:02:16,666
there are no silly questions.
So please feel free to do so.

42
00:02:17,800 --> 00:02:20,800
And yeah,
let's keep this conversation going.

43
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,666
So—value to the player.

44
00:02:23,666 --> 00:02:27,733
The item should enhance gameplay
and provide unique advantages

45
00:02:28,033 --> 00:02:31,933
or offer aesthetic customization
that feels worth the purchase.

46
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:33,833
Appealing design.

47
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:37,700
The items should be visually attractive,
themed to the game,

48
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:41,233
and easy to understand or use.
Fun!

49
00:02:42,266 --> 00:02:46,033
I think we all like to have fun,
so a silly item will definitely go

50
00:02:46,033 --> 00:02:48,233
a long way.

51
00:02:48,233 --> 00:02:51,233
And it just,
I don't know, something to giggle at.

52
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:53,866
It just raises the endorphins

53
00:02:53,866 --> 00:02:56,866
and gets you going.
Alrighty—

54
00:02:57,133 --> 00:03:00,066
Let's look at those examples.

55
00:03:00,066 --> 00:03:02,933
So first up, I have Hardy World Spades.

56
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:05,933
And I chose this,

57
00:03:06,533 --> 00:03:09,533
I chose this because

58
00:03:09,866 --> 00:03:12,966
Hardy has definitely a solid community

59
00:03:12,966 --> 00:03:15,966
and they come in to play spades.

60
00:03:16,066 --> 00:03:19,066
I really like how passionate they are
in that world.

61
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:24,166
And I've seen a lot of people
collect these chairs for gameplay.

62
00:03:24,766 --> 00:03:27,766
They also have these card pickers

63
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:31,933
which I thought was
pretty neat and pretty funny.

64
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:33,266
Alright,

65
00:03:33,266 --> 00:03:36,266
next up—shoutout to HardyWest.

66
00:03:36,466 --> 00:03:39,466
Next up is Cave Survivor by PoppaHoppa.

67
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:42,100
I really liked the setup

68
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,866
for his IWPs—

69
00:03:44,866 --> 00:03:46,966
his assets.

70
00:03:46,966 --> 00:03:49,600
And what was really cute,

71
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:52,900
what really stuck out to me,
was this rubber chicken.

72
00:03:53,033 --> 00:03:58,633
So basically,
the game itself is you have to survive

73
00:03:58,633 --> 00:04:01,833
not getting drowned in a cave
that is filling with water.

74
00:04:02,100 --> 00:04:05,633
And basically, your opponents have to
either kick you into the water

75
00:04:05,633 --> 00:04:09,166
or you're going to have to
accidentally go in.

76
00:04:09,633 --> 00:04:13,600
And getting beat up by a rubber
chicken is really funny.

77
00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:16,800
Next up, we have Lights,

78
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:19,800
Camera, Zombies by WellPlayedStudio.

79
00:04:20,266 --> 00:04:23,266
That is Kyle Render and KaceyMon.

80
00:04:24,100 --> 00:04:26,900
I chose this one because

81
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:29,166
I really found these zombie

82
00:04:29,166 --> 00:04:32,166
masks really funny,

83
00:04:32,366 --> 00:04:35,366
but what's important is how they use them.

84
00:04:35,866 --> 00:04:41,100
So, for example, danger scout, cowboy,
and mafioso

85
00:04:41,533 --> 00:04:44,566
all have the same face but different hats.

86
00:04:45,233 --> 00:04:47,366
And that's a good use of assets.

87
00:04:48,766 --> 00:04:51,466
And so, going lower

88
00:04:51,466 --> 00:04:56,000
you have flower scout, cowgirl, and flapper
and it's the same situation.

89
00:04:56,400 --> 00:04:59,400
And I thought this was a really clever
use of

90
00:05:00,200 --> 00:05:02,466
the space.

91
00:05:02,466 --> 00:05:06,566
And next up would be Battle for Steel City
by RJTheCreator,

92
00:05:06,566 --> 00:05:09,800
and shoutout to king_of_miami

93
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:12,800
And biggie_pauls for the scripting.

94
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:16,433
So here—

95
00:05:16,433 --> 00:05:21,566
What's cool about this
is he used this armor and helmet

96
00:05:22,100 --> 00:05:25,100
and created new skins for them

97
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,633
on each selection.

98
00:05:27,633 --> 00:05:31,333
And that really maximizes
the use of assets

99
00:05:31,733 --> 00:05:35,500
that you have, you make, 
and so on.

100
00:05:35,500 --> 00:05:39,433
You could really expand on just one item
you've created.

101
00:05:40,166 --> 00:05:43,166
Here is an example of the air boards.

102
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,633
And same situation—

103
00:05:46,633 --> 00:05:51,266
You have one item but different texture
loops.

104
00:05:51,266 --> 00:05:56,933
So it really kind of stretches
just one item out for you.

105
00:05:58,633 --> 00:06:01,633
I really like that butterfly skull one.

106
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:02,700
All right.

107
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:06,333
And then last up is Spin
the Bottle by Meta

108
00:06:06,333 --> 00:06:09,300
Jesus.

109
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:12,300
This one
definitely gives—this section right here

110
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:15,066
definitely gives me the sense of fun.

111
00:06:15,066 --> 00:06:17,400
Shout out to emmytr0n

112
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:21,900
for her banana rifle,
which is actually my favorite.

113
00:06:22,766 --> 00:06:25,700
And then you also have this

114
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:28,700
toilet gun right there.

115
00:06:28,833 --> 00:06:33,600
I find it really funny,
and I know the kids do, too.

116
00:06:35,133 --> 00:06:37,500
Samurai Tycoon by Emorgul.

117
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:40,500
I did choose this one because,

118
00:06:41,266 --> 00:06:45,300
first off, I spent a lot of time in there
trying to collect all those swords

119
00:06:45,766 --> 00:06:48,766
and my favorite
is the giant kitchen knife.

120
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:52,466
And... all right.

121
00:06:52,466 --> 00:06:54,800
So, these worlds

122
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:59,766
provide items for
customized gameplay, such as custom

123
00:06:59,766 --> 00:07:04,600
environmental elements,
wearables in many customizable styles,

124
00:07:05,233 --> 00:07:08,400
fun weapons to choose, cool power ups,

125
00:07:08,733 --> 00:07:13,800
and items to use for in-game travel,
such as a hoverboard or a jetpack.

126
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:17,800
And thank you for being here.

127
00:07:17,800 --> 00:07:21,333
Seriously—I said this earlier today,

128
00:07:21,333 --> 00:07:24,433
I'm going to say it again,
for all those that are brand

129
00:07:24,433 --> 00:07:27,866
new to the MHCP, welcome!

130
00:07:28,266 --> 00:07:32,600
And I'm seriously,
seriously thrilled that you are here

131
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:37,066
and I am excited to see what you all make,
especially with this

132
00:07:37,933 --> 00:07:42,600
competition going
or just learning.

133
00:07:42,633 --> 00:07:48,666
Please, definitely post in the Discord
what you're working on,

134
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:52,900
all of your models or everything.

135
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:57,100
Just don't be shy
because we are definitely there to help.

136
00:07:57,633 --> 00:08:00,666
Alrighty! So let's get to it.

137
00:08:02,233 --> 00:08:05,233
So earlier today,

138
00:08:05,766 --> 00:08:07,700
and I actually want to just give you

139
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:11,100
a quick peek of what was made.

140
00:08:14,266 --> 00:08:17,266
We made...

141
00:08:17,866 --> 00:08:20,100
a blaster.

142
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:22,866
We're going to be doing weapons today—

143
00:08:22,866 --> 00:08:23,333
tonight.

144
00:08:24,300 --> 00:08:24,633
Okay,

145
00:08:24,633 --> 00:08:27,633
let's make this axe.

146
00:08:31,766 --> 00:08:32,633
Alrighty.

147
00:08:32,633 --> 00:08:35,633
So I'm going to actually...

148
00:08:36,233 --> 00:08:39,233
going to do this really quick.

149
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Here we are.

150
00:08:49,766 --> 00:08:52,766
Okie dokie.

151
00:08:54,166 --> 00:08:57,833
So, today
what I will be doing is teaching you

152
00:08:57,833 --> 00:09:00,833
how to model
with the subdivision modifier.

153
00:09:04,400 --> 00:09:07,400
Hold on a sec. So—

154
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,500
the reason why I'm using the subdivision

155
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:13,500
modifier is because

156
00:09:13,866 --> 00:09:18,366
number one:
it's a really fun tool to use.

157
00:09:18,833 --> 00:09:23,933
And number two: we are going to make this
model low poly. Keeping it low poly,

158
00:09:24,266 --> 00:09:27,266
as low as we can.

159
00:09:28,033 --> 00:09:31,033
So, let's get to it.

160
00:09:31,433 --> 00:09:34,433
So first up,

161
00:09:34,666 --> 00:09:36,533
I'm going to go ahead and press Shift-A,

162
00:09:36,533 --> 00:09:39,800
and I'm going to create my cube.

163
00:09:42,066 --> 00:09:45,066
And I’m going to bring 
this axe over

164
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:48,900
so we can see it.

165
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:55,800
Hold on one second.

166
00:09:58,900 --> 00:10:00,066
Okay.

167
00:10:00,066 --> 00:10:01,333
She's going to stay right there.

168
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:04,600
Alrighty.

169
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:07,600
So, first things first.

170
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:10,166
I'm going to go ahead and take this cube

171
00:10:10,166 --> 00:10:13,166
and make it a sphere.

172
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:18,533
I'm going to add a new modifier
over here on the right hand side.

173
00:10:18,566 --> 00:10:22,633
We're going to click on the wrench
and add that modifier.

174
00:10:22,833 --> 00:10:24,033
Pressing search,

175
00:10:24,033 --> 00:10:27,666
I'm going to then to type out
subdivision.

176
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:30,233
It's at the top
because I've been using it.

177
00:10:30,233 --> 00:10:32,500
So I'm going to just click that.

178
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:34,833
And there we are—look at that!

179
00:10:34,833 --> 00:10:40,300
We magically turned this cube
into a sphere

180
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:43,000
Alrighty.

181
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,300
So now, let's

182
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,866
make it into something.

183
00:10:46,866 --> 00:10:49,800
I'm going to go ahead and press Tab

184
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:52,166
to Object mode.

185
00:10:52,166 --> 00:10:55,033
I mean Edit mode. Sorry, my bad.

186
00:10:55,033 --> 00:10:59,933
Then what I'm going to do
is I think I'm going to just start off—

187
00:11:01,766 --> 00:11:02,466
I'm not going

188
00:11:02,466 --> 00:11:05,533
to make a tube for this guy.

189
00:11:05,566 --> 00:11:08,666
I'm going to just stay in this
subdivision

190
00:11:08,666 --> 00:11:11,666
modifier for the entire build.

191
00:11:11,700 --> 00:11:12,266
Alrighty.

192
00:11:12,266 --> 00:11:15,566
So, what I'm going to do
is I'm going to do Face Select mode,

193
00:11:16,633 --> 00:11:19,633
and then I'm going to select this
top face.

194
00:11:19,666 --> 00:11:21,766
Alrighty.

195
00:11:21,766 --> 00:11:24,766
Pressing G
and then Z, I'm going to bring it up.

196
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:27,433
All right.

197
00:11:27,433 --> 00:11:29,566
However,

198
00:11:29,566 --> 00:11:31,200
now we have an issue.

199
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:34,200
Well first off, I'm going
to just scale this down a little bit.

200
00:11:37,733 --> 00:11:40,733
Just a smidge.

201
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:46,400
Where are you?

202
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,400
[...]

203
00:11:53,766 --> 00:11:56,766
Oh, what’s going on?

204
00:11:57,233 --> 00:12:00,233
Why did that twist?

205
00:12:00,866 --> 00:12:03,000
All right, funky things are happening.

206
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,133
But that's all right.

207
00:12:04,133 --> 00:12:05,366
Okay.

208
00:12:05,366 --> 00:12:07,533
Now, the thing about the subdivision

209
00:12:07,533 --> 00:12:11,400
modifier
is it's basically taking that square

210
00:12:12,133 --> 00:12:14,700
and it's turning it into like a

211
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:17,800
a malleable clay, right?

212
00:12:18,733 --> 00:12:21,733
But now this clay needs

213
00:12:22,033 --> 00:12:25,033
supports for it to take shape.

214
00:12:25,033 --> 00:12:29,800
So what I'm going to do
is I'm going to do Control-R,

215
00:12:30,633 --> 00:12:33,633
and then I'm going to create that support.

216
00:12:33,800 --> 00:12:36,900
As you can see, now I have

217
00:12:37,966 --> 00:12:39,300
some geometry

218
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:42,300
being held up at this edge here.

219
00:12:42,300 --> 00:12:44,400
I'm going to do the same for the bottom.

220
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:49,366
I'm going to do Control-R 
to create an edge loop,

221
00:12:49,766 --> 00:12:52,766
and then I'm going to bring that down.

222
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:56,400
All right, sweet.

223
00:12:57,433 --> 00:13:00,433
Actually—

224
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:04,000
let me go ahead and

225
00:13:05,233 --> 00:13:08,233
bring this up a bit.

226
00:13:09,933 --> 00:13:12,000
Okay.

227
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:14,466
G and Z.

228
00:13:14,466 --> 00:13:18,033
This blue line is the Z axis.

229
00:13:18,800 --> 00:13:21,833
So, as you can see, I'm pressing G, Z.

230
00:13:21,833 --> 00:13:25,600
And this is for those who are brand
new to Blender.

231
00:13:26,033 --> 00:13:29,833
We are pulling up and down on that Z axis.

232
00:13:30,066 --> 00:13:32,700
All right. Sweet.

233
00:13:32,700 --> 00:13:34,933
Now what we want to do

234
00:13:34,933 --> 00:13:39,300
is we want to make this bottom part here.

235
00:13:40,333 --> 00:13:43,300
Now normally, I would probably

236
00:13:43,300 --> 00:13:46,300
create new geo and just add it

237
00:13:46,400 --> 00:13:48,766
and actually, I think I will do that.

238
00:13:50,833 --> 00:13:52,633
Yeah.

239
00:13:52,633 --> 00:13:55,100
Okay. So— 

240
00:13:55,100 --> 00:13:59,900
Then, I'm going to Tab back
into Object mode and create a new object.

241
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:03,200
Shift-A,

242
00:14:03,266 --> 00:14:06,266
then the cube.

243
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:09,600
I'm going to go ahead
and add that modifier

244
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:12,600
because we are practicing
with the subdivision modifier.

245
00:14:13,800 --> 00:14:15,600
Another thing to note is

246
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:18,600
when you're building
with the subdivision modifier,

247
00:14:19,633 --> 00:14:22,933
if you were to bring up the levels,

248
00:14:23,266 --> 00:14:25,933
it can get really expensive

249
00:14:25,933 --> 00:14:28,600
really quick and we do not want that.

250
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:32,433
So, we're going to leave it at one
and keep these

251
00:14:33,033 --> 00:14:36,333
models very,
very simple and low poly.

252
00:14:36,333 --> 00:14:39,333
So putting this aside,

253
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:42,666
I'm going to go ahead

254
00:14:42,666 --> 00:14:46,866
and on my keyboard,
if you are a Windows user, you press three.

255
00:14:47,366 --> 00:14:49,866
That way you can have

256
00:14:49,866 --> 00:14:52,866
what is called the side orthographic view.

257
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:57,966
Then I'm going to go ahead
and press Tab to go into Edit mode.

258
00:15:02,666 --> 00:15:03,066
I'm going to go

259
00:15:03,066 --> 00:15:06,266
ahead and turn on X-ray mode.

260
00:15:06,266 --> 00:15:10,300
And what X-ray mode allows me to do
is it allows me

261
00:15:10,300 --> 00:15:15,333
to select
