00:30:29,266 --> 00:30:32,266
I’m going to do G, Z. 

527
00:30:32,400 --> 00:30:34,500
Extruding—there we are.

528
00:30:34,500 --> 00:30:37,066
Problem solved.

529
00:30:37,066 --> 00:30:40,066
I’m going to scale by the Y,

530
00:30:41,133 --> 00:30:44,000
and I'm going to press G and then Y.

531
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:45,433
And then I'm going to bring that back.

532
00:30:46,566 --> 00:30:47,166
There we are.

533
00:30:47,166 --> 00:30:50,000
Now we're taking shape.

534
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:54,700
Now we in the business. 
Okay, cool.

535
00:30:55,500 --> 00:30:57,866
I'm going to do
pretty much the same thing on the bottom,

536
00:30:57,866 --> 00:31:00,800
and then we'll model it some more.

537
00:31:00,800 --> 00:31:03,800
I'm going to click on this bottom face,

538
00:31:04,100 --> 00:31:07,100
pressing E to extrude.

539
00:31:08,033 --> 00:31:11,100
And then I'm going to scale by the Y.

540
00:31:12,833 --> 00:31:15,833
And then I'm going to press G and then Y,

541
00:31:15,966 --> 00:31:18,966
and then bring this back.

542
00:31:20,966 --> 00:31:23,966
Alrighty.

543
00:31:24,766 --> 00:31:25,633
Pretty, pretty good.

544
00:31:25,633 --> 00:31:28,633
I'd like to work on this geo here, though.

545
00:31:35,700 --> 00:31:37,366
I'm going to do—

546
00:31:37,366 --> 00:31:39,800
To select the entire edge loop,

547
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:42,800
I'm going to press Shift-Alt,

548
00:31:43,066 --> 00:31:44,733
and then I'm going to press G

549
00:31:44,733 --> 00:31:48,600
and then Y,
and kind of really sandwich that

550
00:31:49,400 --> 00:31:51,933
edge loop to the next.

551
00:31:51,933 --> 00:31:54,933
That way I have a harsher

552
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:58,833
line...

553
00:31:58,833 --> 00:31:59,700
between...

554
00:32:01,400 --> 00:32:04,400
this part and the blade.

555
00:32:10,933 --> 00:32:11,900
Alrighty.

556
00:32:11,900 --> 00:32:15,866
So, then I'm going to select this face.
I want to bring this out a little bit.

557
00:32:17,366 --> 00:32:18,600
I'm going to press G,

558
00:32:18,600 --> 00:32:21,233
and then Y,

559
00:32:21,233 --> 00:32:24,066
and then bring that out.

560
00:32:24,066 --> 00:32:26,633
Oh, that's huge!

561
00:32:26,633 --> 00:32:28,533
And that's fine.

562
00:32:28,533 --> 00:32:31,533
I’m going to go ahead and select
this entire thing.

563
00:32:32,833 --> 00:32:35,833
Actually, no. I'm not in X-ray mode.

564
00:32:36,800 --> 00:32:39,800
X-ray mode.

565
00:32:40,566 --> 00:32:43,566
And then I'll do that again.

566
00:32:45,066 --> 00:32:48,066
And press S to scale.

567
00:32:49,200 --> 00:32:51,800
<i>Now I'm messing it up. </i>

568
00:32:51,800 --> 00:32:54,800
<i>It's all right.</i>

569
00:32:55,700 --> 00:32:59,066
And really,

570
00:32:59,400 --> 00:33:02,400
3D modeling is problem-solving.

571
00:33:02,700 --> 00:33:06,266
You find yourself doing more problem-
solving than anything

572
00:33:06,966 --> 00:33:08,266
throughout the process.

573
00:33:08,266 --> 00:33:10,600
To me, that's the fun part.

574
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:13,600
Getting things to just work,

575
00:33:14,833 --> 00:33:17,333
you know?

576
00:33:17,333 --> 00:33:19,033
I’m going to
try to scale it from there—

577
00:33:19,033 --> 00:33:20,700
All right.

578
00:33:20,700 --> 00:33:22,100
Solid.

579
00:33:22,100 --> 00:33:26,200
I'm going to press G and then Y. 
Bring that up a little more.

580
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:28,966
G, Z a little bit.

581
00:33:33,200 --> 00:33:36,200
Alrighty.

582
00:33:37,133 --> 00:33:40,133
Take that out of X-ray mode.

583
00:33:40,166 --> 00:33:43,166
And let's take a good
look at what we have so far.

584
00:33:45,433 --> 00:33:45,900
Alrighty.

585
00:33:45,900 --> 00:33:47,933
What do you think?

586
00:33:47,933 --> 00:33:50,933
Sound off in the chat!

587
00:33:51,466 --> 00:33:54,466
<i>Let's get this party started.</i>

588
00:33:57,166 --> 00:33:59,400
Yeah.

589
00:33:59,400 --> 00:34:00,733
Well—

590
00:34:00,733 --> 00:34:02,700
I can't wait to see what you guys make.

591
00:34:02,700 --> 00:34:06,333
Seriously,
when you guys practice this definitely

592
00:34:07,966 --> 00:34:11,300
post in the Discord. Post
in #what-im-building.

593
00:34:11,866 --> 00:34:14,533
That's the best place to post your

594
00:34:14,533 --> 00:34:17,533
3D modeling
and what you're working on.

595
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:21,400
I love to see what people are making,

596
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:24,400
especially on the art side of things,

597
00:34:24,433 --> 00:34:27,833
so super-geeked about that.

598
00:34:27,866 --> 00:34:30,866
I definitely am excited for you guys

599
00:34:31,166 --> 00:34:34,166
and excited you're here.

600
00:34:34,366 --> 00:34:38,066
All right,
so let's get to the rest of this.

601
00:34:39,866 --> 00:34:42,866
I’m going to go ahead...

602
00:34:44,466 --> 00:34:45,200
I'm going to go ahead

603
00:34:45,200 --> 00:34:48,400
and press
Tab to go back into that Edit mode.

604
00:34:48,900 --> 00:34:50,933
And let's go on this side now.

605
00:34:52,866 --> 00:34:55,066
I'm going to press this face here,

606
00:34:55,066 --> 00:34:58,266
and then I'm going to press that magic
I button.

607
00:34:59,766 --> 00:35:02,766
I for insert.

608
00:35:02,900 --> 00:35:05,900
I'm eyeballing it now because, you know,

609
00:35:06,066 --> 00:35:08,900
we're making it fantastic.

610
00:35:08,900 --> 00:35:11,900
Alrighty.

611
00:35:12,833 --> 00:35:16,200
I'm going to go ahead
and go into orthographic view,

612
00:35:16,200 --> 00:35:17,766
so I can see what I'm doing.

613
00:35:17,766 --> 00:35:21,500
Pressing E to extrude, and

614
00:35:23,066 --> 00:35:26,066
that seems about right.

615
00:35:26,066 --> 00:35:27,233
Now let's ensure

616
00:35:27,233 --> 00:35:30,600
that there is enough support
for this edge.

617
00:35:30,633 --> 00:35:35,100
So what I'm going to do
is I'm going to press Control-R

618
00:35:36,400 --> 00:35:38,733
and then I'm going to bring this support
down.

619
00:35:38,733 --> 00:35:41,666
<i>[vocalizing]</i>

620
00:35:41,666 --> 00:35:44,666
All right, and...

621
00:35:48,200 --> 00:35:49,166
One more support—

622
00:35:49,166 --> 00:35:52,300
Control-R, bringing it all the way up.

623
00:35:54,500 --> 00:35:55,033
All right,

624
00:35:55,033 --> 00:35:58,033
solid.

625
00:35:58,966 --> 00:36:01,100
You just have to take your time.

626
00:36:01,100 --> 00:36:03,933
I promise—the more you practice,

627
00:36:03,933 --> 00:36:08,866
the more a lot of this stuff
becomes mindless.

628
00:36:10,200 --> 00:36:12,766
Most likely,
if I were to do this on my own,

629
00:36:12,766 --> 00:36:14,033
it would have been done already.

630
00:36:14,033 --> 00:36:19,266
But I am explaining things as I go,
and you're going to get to that point.

631
00:36:19,266 --> 00:36:22,766
Like, you really just have to be in it,
practicing,

632
00:36:22,766 --> 00:36:25,766
doing it as much as you can. 
Give yourself

633
00:36:26,266 --> 00:36:27,966
at least 20 minutes a day.

634
00:36:27,966 --> 00:36:32,733
Just open up Blender—
Play with the default cube,

635
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:36,366
you know? I know that's blasphemous,
but play with that cube.

636
00:36:36,433 --> 00:36:37,533
Make it into something.

637
00:36:37,533 --> 00:36:40,533
Just press extrude
until something makes sense.

638
00:36:41,033 --> 00:36:45,033
And I kid you not, the more you do that,
the more you'll get comfortable

639
00:36:45,433 --> 00:36:48,366
with at least doing some light

640
00:36:48,366 --> 00:36:51,366
modeling in Blender.

641
00:36:53,200 --> 00:36:56,000
All right, so—

642
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:58,200
<i>[vocalizing]</i>

643
00:36:58,200 --> 00:36:59,666
Am I in? No I'm not.

644
00:36:59,666 --> 00:37:04,400
All right, so I'm going to go
ahead and select these guys.

645
00:37:06,566 --> 00:37:09,566
I do realize that this needs to be

646
00:37:09,833 --> 00:37:11,366
thinner, but it's all right.

647
00:37:11,366 --> 00:37:14,366
I'm going to press S to scale.

648
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:19,400
Actually, I'm not mad at it, but,

649
00:37:19,466 --> 00:37:22,466
I'll work it out afterwards.

650
00:37:24,500 --> 00:37:28,666
I’m going to go ahead and 
grab this face.

651
00:37:31,266 --> 00:37:34,800
Then I'm going to go ahead
and E to extrude,

652
00:37:38,266 --> 00:37:41,133
and I have my reasons.

653
00:37:41,133 --> 00:37:43,366
I'd like to make that little lip

654
00:37:43,366 --> 00:37:46,133
that goes before

655
00:37:46,133 --> 00:37:49,133
the blade,

656
00:37:49,266 --> 00:37:49,466
but

657
00:37:49,466 --> 00:37:53,600
before I do that, I'm
definitely going to model the blade first.

658
00:37:53,600 --> 00:37:56,600
I think that's the way
I'm going to go about this.

659
00:37:58,200 --> 00:37:59,933
Yeah.

660
00:37:59,933 --> 00:38:01,866
Good idea guys. Good idea.

661
00:38:01,866 --> 00:38:04,100
All right, let's get to it.

662
00:38:04,100 --> 00:38:07,200
So I'm going to go ahead and press E
to extrude.

663
00:38:12,933 --> 00:38:15,566
Go on up top here,

664
00:38:15,566 --> 00:38:18,566
pressing E to extrude.

665
00:38:22,233 --> 00:38:26,100
E to extrude again,

666
00:38:26,400 --> 00:38:28,866
and then I'm going to scale it by the Y.

667
00:38:29,866 --> 00:38:31,033
And then I'm going to

668
00:38:31,033 --> 00:38:34,466
go ahead and G,

669
00:38:36,266 --> 00:38:39,266
Y, and bring that back.

670
00:38:40,966 --> 00:38:41,466
Look at that—

671
00:38:41,466 --> 00:38:44,466
it's already looking dangerous.

672
00:38:44,666 --> 00:38:47,766
Okay, I'm going to select this bottom face
here...

673
00:38:50,633 --> 00:38:53,633
E to extrude...

674
00:38:56,266 --> 00:38:59,266
And then, E to extrude again.

675
00:39:03,666 --> 00:39:05,433
Pressing S to scale

676
00:39:05,433 --> 00:39:09,466
and Y—make it nice and sharp. 
G, 

677
00:39:09,600 --> 00:39:12,600
and then Y.

678
00:39:13,333 --> 00:39:15,566
Fantastic.

679
00:39:15,566 --> 00:39:17,933
Now, I'm going to make my adjustments.

680
00:39:17,933 --> 00:39:20,933
Select this, pressing G,

681
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:24,000
and then Y.

682
00:39:24,966 --> 00:39:27,900
<i>Ooh... </i>dangerous.

683
00:39:27,900 --> 00:39:30,100
Okay.

684
00:39:30,100 --> 00:39:33,733
That's looking great,
I think. How's it look to you guys?

685
00:39:33,733 --> 00:39:36,733
Looking good?

686
00:39:41,233 --> 00:39:44,233
Yeah.

687
00:39:47,233 --> 00:39:50,233
Okay.

688
00:39:50,466 --> 00:39:51,666
What I want to do for this

689
00:39:51,666 --> 00:39:55,100
section is start to create some extra geo,

690
00:39:55,133 --> 00:39:58,133
so I'm going to do Alt-E

691
00:39:58,800 --> 00:40:02,000
to extrude along faces.

692
00:40:03,300 --> 00:40:06,100
As you can see now I have this little

693
00:40:06,100 --> 00:40:08,300
band forming here.

694
00:40:14,100 --> 00:40:14,333
Yeah,

695
00:40:14,333 --> 00:40:17,333
that's good.

696
00:40:18,300 --> 00:40:19,333
It's not squared off

697
00:40:19,333 --> 00:40:23,366
because I mean theoretically,
if I really wanted it to be square,

698
00:40:23,366 --> 00:40:26,366
I would have to put some more
geo in between.

699
00:40:27,100 --> 00:40:31,333
But I like the fact that it still feels
low poly, so I'm going to

700
00:40:31,900 --> 00:40:34,900
I'm going to keep it
the way it is for now.

701
00:40:36,300 --> 00:40:39,300
Yeah.

702
00:40:39,533 --> 00:40:40,933
Let's see what happens

703
00:40:40,933 --> 00:40:43,933
if I put another edge loop in this corner
here.

704
00:40:44,733 --> 00:40:47,733
Control-R and

705
00:40:48,233 --> 00:40:50,933
squeeze that in there.

706
00:40:50,933 --> 00:40:53,633
Yeah, that's a nice little detail.

707
00:40:53,633 --> 00:40:56,633
I'm going to go ahead
and do the same on the other side.

708
00:40:57,000 --> 00:40:59,033
Control-R

709
00:40:59,033 --> 00:41:02,033
and squish.

710
00:41:02,066 --> 00:41:04,433
Very good.

711
00:41:04,433 --> 00:41:05,733
Yeah.

712
00:41:05,733 --> 00:41:08,733
Looking dangerous.

713
00:41:08,866 --> 00:41:09,966
Face select mode—

714
00:41:09,966 --> 00:41:14,566
I kind of kind of want to make this
a little more pointier at the top.

715
00:41:14,600 --> 00:41:17,233
I don't know about you
guys, but I like it pointy.

716
00:41:18,233 --> 00:41:23,266
G, and then Y,

717
00:41:23,500 --> 00:41:25,833
but then I want to bring it G, Z.

718
00:41:25,833 --> 00:41:28,833
I want to bring it up a bit.

719
00:41:30,700 --> 00:41:31,066
All right.

720
00:41:31,066 --> 00:41:33,933
Sweet.

721
00:41:33,933 --> 00:41:36,200
Now, what I'd like to do...

722
00:41:36,200 --> 00:41:39,300
I’m not going to make it circular
but I'm definitely going to do a little

723
00:41:39,300 --> 00:41:40,866
something here.

724
00:41:40,866 --> 00:41:43,866
So, I'm going to select this face.

725
00:41:44,466 --> 00:41:47,466
I'm going to press I to inset,

726
00:41:49,466 --> 00:41:52,466
and then

727
00:41:53,033 --> 00:41:56,033
I to inset again.

728
00:41:56,466 --> 00:41:59,566
Then, I'd like to E to extrude.

729
00:42:01,400 --> 00:42:03,266
Oh yeah, it came out circular anyways.

730
00:42:03,266 --> 00:42:06,266
That's fantastic.

731
00:42:06,300 --> 00:42:08,100
Very nice.

732
00:42:08,100 --> 00:42:11,100
Let's do the same on the other side,
just for practice.

733
00:42:11,866 --> 00:42:12,466
Alrighty,

734
00:42:12,466 --> 00:42:15,600
so I'm going to do I to inset.

735
00:42:18,466 --> 00:42:21,133
I for inset again,

736
00:42:21,133 --> 00:42:24,133
and then I'm going to press E to extrude.

737
00:42:27,333 --> 00:42:28,666
Alrighty.

738
00:42:28,666 --> 00:42:31,500
So, I'm going to go ahead
and click out of this

739
00:42:31,500 --> 00:42:34,500
by pressing Tab to go into Object mode.

740
00:42:34,833 --> 00:42:37,166
Tab is your friend. Please,

741
00:42:38,400 --> 00:42:43,300
please, definitely utilize that Tab hotkey

742
00:42:43,366 --> 00:42:46,800
because it will make your workflow
a lot quicker.

743
00:42:47,766 --> 00:42:49,666
Alrighty.

744
00:42:49,666 --> 00:42:52,666
What do you guys think about that design?

745
00:42:54,266 --> 00:42:56,833
Sound off in the chat.

746
00:42:56,833 --> 00:42:59,000
<i>Talk to me. Talk to me.</i>

747
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:01,700
I think it looks good!

748
00:43:01,700 --> 00:43:03,933
Yeah...

749
00:43:03,933 --> 00:43:04,466
And guess what?

750
00:43:04,466 --> 00:43:06,600
You could do it too.

751
00:43:06,600 --> 00:43:09,000
You can do it too.

752
00:43:09,000 --> 00:43:10,533
You got the magic.

753
00:43:10,533 --> 00:43:13,533
I believe in you, superstars.

754
00:43:14,100 --> 00:43:16,100
Yeah.

755
00:43:16,100 --> 00:43:18,500
There's a little craziness going on here.

756
00:43:18,500 --> 00:43:19,400
Let me check this out

757
00:43:19,400 --> 00:43:22,400
really quick. Tab—

758
00:43:25,400 --> 00:43:28,400
[...]
Maybe it's just me.

759
00:43:30,900 --> 00:43:36,566
Maybe if I were to select this entire loop
by pressing Shift-Alt,

760
00:43:36,600 --> 00:43:39,800
and then just nudging it
a little closer.

761
00:43:40,300 --> 00:43:43,300
G, Y, and let's get that

762
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:45,100
sandwiched in better

763
00:43:45,100 --> 00:43:46,700
there.

764
00:43:46,700 --> 00:43:49,166
All right, cool.

765
00:43:49,166 --> 00:43:52,166
Okie dokie.

766
00:43:53,933 --> 00:43:54,133
Yeah,

767
00:43:54,133 --> 00:43:54,566
that's it.

768
00:43:54,566 --> 00:43:57,200
It's a matter of practicing those hotkeys.

769
00:43:57,200 --> 00:44:00,200
I did actually make a hotkey sheet.

770
00:44:00,633 --> 00:44:02,833
It's in the library.

771
00:44:02,833 --> 00:44:04,700
It's called, “SpaceGlitter’s

772
00:44:04,700 --> 00:44:07,633
Guide to the Blenderverse.” And it's—

773
00:44:07,633 --> 00:44:11,366
I kept it really simple and short
so that it's easy to navigate.

774
00:44:13,200 --> 00:44:15,600
All right. So—

775
00:44:15,600 --> 00:44:17,033
What do you guys think, you want—

776
00:44:17,033 --> 00:44:20,033
You want to texture this?

777
00:44:22,200 --> 00:44:24,500
Let's do it.

778
00:44:24,500 --> 00:44:25,100
Yeah.

779
00:44:25,100 --> 00:44:28,100
Let's texture this guy.

780
00:44:29,166 --> 00:44:31,066
I like it.

781
00:44:31,066 --> 00:44:32,200
I do.

782
00:44:32,200 --> 00:44:35,200
Okay, so.

783
00:44:37,033 --> 00:44:39,333
For you amazing, wonderful people,

784
00:44:39,333 --> 00:44:42,333
I created something extra special.

785
00:44:43,200 --> 00:44:46,200
I created a trim sheet just for you.

786
00:44:47,800 --> 00:44:51,266
In this trim sheet,
there are different options

787
00:44:51,266 --> 00:44:54,266
to use.

788
00:44:55,733 --> 00:44:58,733
In this section, you have your roughness.

789
00:45:02,666 --> 00:45:06,133
Basically, there's no shine
in this section and I'll show you how

790
00:45:06,133 --> 00:45:07,633
it works.

791
00:45:07,633 --> 00:45:11,066
In this section,
you get your shiny, plasticky material.

792
00:45:12,033 --> 00:45:16,100
And this is all one, big sheet
